From b676f0ef3a5d011461e17da2161b1678416daf8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isoriano1968 <81116077+isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:36:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] NNNNN usbvc: frame size/interval enumeration, frame based
 formats, poll(2)

V4L2 applications such as Chromium's video capture find the frame sizes
and rates of a camera with VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES and
VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMEINTERVALS, and poll(2) the device before each
VIDIOC_DQBUF. usbvc had neither.

- VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES and VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMEINTERVALS from the frame
  descriptors the driver already parses: discrete sizes; discrete or
  stepwise/continuous intervals as reduced fractions of a second.
- chpoll(9E): POLLIN when a buffer is done (mmap I/O or read(2)),
  POLLHUP when the camera is unplugged.
- UVC frame based formats (VS_FORMAT_FRAME_BASED: MJPEG, H.264). Their
  frame descriptors keep dwDefaultFrameInterval and bFrameIntervalType
  at other offsets, so both are now decoded per frame at attach time.
- Format GUIDs: I420, YV12, UYVY, M420, Y800, Y16 besides YUY2 and NV12.
- VIDIOC_QUERYCAP sets device_caps and V4L2_CAP_DEVICE_CAPS.
- VIDIOC_S_FMT fails with EINVAL, not EFAULT, for an unknown format.
- The default format no longer assumes frames[0] has a descriptor.
- sys/videodev2.h: the frame size/interval enumeration, device_caps,
  the v4l2_pix_format colour fields (ycbcr_enc, quantization, xfer_func),
  colour enums, camera class controls, events, more pixel formats and
  buffer flags, with Linux V4L2's sizes, offsets and values.
